# Overview

In this project, I set up a Java web application entirely in the cloud using Amazon EC2.

This is Part 1 of a 6-day DevOps challenge where the final goal is to build a complete CI/CD pipeline.  
Before automation, I first needed a working cloud-hosted application.

By the end of this project, I successfully:

- Launched and secured an EC2 instance
- Connected via SSH using a key pair
- Installed Apache Maven
- Installed Amazon Corretto 8 (Java 8)
- Generated a Java web application using Maven
- Connected VS Code to EC2 using Remote - SSH
- Edited application files using both an IDE and nano (terminal)

