# Step 5 — Install Apache Maven

## What is Maven?

Apache Maven is a build tool and dependency manager for Java applications.

It:
- Compiles code
- Downloads dependencies
- Packages applications
- Generates starter project templates (archetypes)

Maven must be installed inside the EC2 instance because the project is built in the cloud.

## Install Maven

```bash
wget https://archive.apache.org/dist/maven/maven-3/3.5.2/binaries/apache-maven-3.5.2-bin.tar.gz
sudo tar -xzf apache-maven-3.5.2-bin.tar.gz -C /opt
echo "export PATH=/opt/apache-maven-3.5.2/bin:$PATH" >> ~/.bashrc
source ~/.bashrc
```

If wget was missing:

```bash
sudo yum install wget -y
```

Verify installation:

```bash
mvn -v
```

